From: Bjarne <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:14:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: connect to the launcher after the first unlock

LauncherProxyService checks at boot whether the recents provider's service resolves and never
again unless the package changes. Lawnchair's service isn't direct boot aware, because Lawnchair
keeps its settings in credential encrypted storage, so with a PIN set it didn't resolve at boot and
gestures and the navigation handle stayed missing. Re-check when the user unlocks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/com/android/systemui/LauncherProxyService.java         | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/LauncherProxyService.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/LauncherProxyService.java
index e6ad618d5af0972cfa69787ff4c54eeb3196ba4d..fd750e6255ba183d2e582ce32e64b97df32fc49f 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/LauncherProxyService.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/LauncherProxyService.java
@@ -546,6 +546,9 @@ public class LauncherProxyService implements CallbackController<LauncherProxyLis
         @Override
         public void onReceive(Context context, Intent intent) {
             if (Objects.equals(intent.getAction(), Intent.ACTION_USER_UNLOCKED)) {
+                // Graphite: Lawnchair's service isn't direct boot aware, so it didn't resolve
+                // before the unlock. Check again, or the launcher would never be connected.
+                updateEnabledState();
                 // Start the launcher connection to the launcher service
                 // Connect if user hasn't connected yet
                 if (getProxy() == null) {
